WEBVTT

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.130
Start running from the beginning,

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.130
Zero kara kakedashite

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:08.500
with nothing but your emotions in your hands.

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:08.500
Omoi dake wo dakishimete

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.890
Just keep running...

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.890
Sonomama kakenukete

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:18.350
I'm always watching you from here.

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:18.350
Itsumo koko de mitsumeteru

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:42.300
Hajimete deatta hi no manazashi wasurenai

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:42.300
I still remember your expression the day we first met.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:49.190
Taiyou mitai ni kokoro wo terashitekureta

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:49.190
It lit up my heart like the sun.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:56.960
Asu no yukue sagashite nayandeiru nara

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:56.960
If you're anxious about where to go tomorrow,

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:06.890
Ima kimi no tame ni akari ni naritai yo

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:06.890
I want to become a beacon to you.

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.010
Zero kara tobidatte

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.010
Start flying from the beginning.

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:16.380
Ima no kimi wo toki hanachi

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:16.380
Let go of your current self...

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:19.730
Mugen ni habataite

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:19.730
and fly towards infinity.

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:23.600
Donna toki mo mimaru yo

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:23.600
I will always watch over you...

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:29.510
Kitto zutto tooku made

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:29.510
no matter how far you fly.

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:36.870
Maya's newest play is <i>The Forgotten Wilderness</i>,

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:42.570
in which she plays a girl raised by wolves.

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:51.790
How will Maya, the girl with a thousand masks,

00:01:51.790 --> 00:01:58.280
learn the heart of Jane, the untamed wolf girl?

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:06.080
Episode 40 - Jane, the Wolf Girl

00:02:14.990 --> 00:02:17.140
I brought you some food, Jane.

00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:21.760
"Don't be afraid."

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:25.110
"Go ahead, eat."

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:30.860
"I won't tease you."

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:44.100
One month later!

00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:48.300
"Are you starting to get used to me, Jane?"

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:51.210
"This place isn't so bad, is it?"

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:54.400
"Unlike out there in the wilderness, there's no cold wind blowing,

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:57.090
and you don't have to catch your own food either."

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:01.020
"And humans have a rich language too."

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:14.140
"Her eyes... her movements..."

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:17.930
"She's not as wary now, but she still hasn't accepted me fully."

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:19.300
"I understand."

00:03:22.030 --> 00:03:24.140
Next scene! Two months later!

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:28.780
"She's waiting for me?"

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:35.520
"I see. She knew I was coming because she heard my footsteps and the sound of the door opening."

00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:42.870
"We're two months on...

00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:47.070
and I can definitely tell that time has changed for her."

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:48.420
"I won't give up."

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:51.110
All right, let's stop there.

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:57.930
That's good enough for now. If we keep this up, you'll improve over time.

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:05.300
"Try to say it, Jane."

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:07.320
"Move your jaw."

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:08.100
"Jane."

00:04:09.990 --> 00:04:11.050
"Say Jane."

00:04:11.590 --> 00:04:12.800
"Go on. Say it."

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:15.490
"You are Jane!"

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:18.110
"You have to move your jaw."

00:04:25.190 --> 00:04:26.260
Maya...

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:33.270
Sakurakouji!

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:35.830
Sakurakouji!

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:42.060
Good work today.

00:04:43.130 --> 00:04:44.670
Hang on a second.

00:04:44.670 --> 00:04:46.190
I've got something for you.

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:51.040
These are from my fan!

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:54.630
I was also asked to give you this.

00:04:58.370 --> 00:05:00.510
It's a makeup case!

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:05.410
"I wish you success with your new play.

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:08.370
"I am really looking forward to this one."

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:09.930
"From Your Fan."

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:31.000
Could you please give this to the man...

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:33.090
who always sends me these purple roses?

00:05:33.090 --> 00:05:36.420
It's a collection of stage photos from my plays so far.

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:39.430
I'm sure it will please him greatly.

00:05:39.430 --> 00:05:41.380
I'm glad!

00:05:45.020 --> 00:05:47.000
Well then, I should get going.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:48.770
Thank you!

00:05:54.390 --> 00:05:56.620
How did this one fall out?

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:18.510
What should I do?

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:32.570
The elevator's coming down.

00:06:36.390 --> 00:06:38.300
These are the minutes from the meeting,

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:42.230
and here's the research data regarding our new top-secret project.

00:06:43.810 --> 00:06:46.730
And there's this: It's a thank you present.

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:50.150
She was very happy.

00:06:50.150 --> 00:06:51.460
Is that so?

00:06:51.460 --> 00:06:53.230
I will take my leave now.

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:10.850
Mr. Hayami, what are you doing here?

00:07:10.850 --> 00:07:12.280
What a coincidence!

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:15.300
But what are <i>you</i> doing here, little one?

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:18.250
Oh, nothing really!

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:21.650
I thought I saw someone I knew in here.

00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:25.810
By the way, have you heard any news about Ms. Tsukikage?

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:30.130
Nothing yet. Have you heard anything?

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:33.480
I looked everywhere, but I still can't find her.

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:37.530
You'll be the first to know if anything comes up, little one.

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:41.410
Um, Mr. Hayami!

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:43.510
Is it true that you had a meeting for a prospective arranged marriage?

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:45.130
It is.

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:52.720
I've only ever seen her picture in a weekly magazine, but I think she's very pretty.

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:56.220
She's too pretty for someone like me.

00:07:57.810 --> 00:08:00.310
Are you going to marry her?

00:08:02.470 --> 00:08:05.040
What's wrong? You look pale!

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:06.770
I wish you all the happiness in the world!

00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:12.340
Is she jealous?

00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:14.980
She couldn't possibly have feelings for me...

00:08:19.820 --> 00:08:22.330
Mr. President, what's the meaning of this?!

00:08:22.330 --> 00:08:25.600
How dare you drop four of my actors from my play?

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:27.170
What are you talking about?

00:08:27.170 --> 00:08:29.890
They left of their own volition.

00:08:31.460 --> 00:08:33.330
What do you mean?

00:08:33.330 --> 00:08:36.950
You really have no idea how your actors feel about you, do you?

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:41.630
Think about how you treated them during rehearsals!

00:08:42.230 --> 00:08:43.800
You call that pronunciation?!

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:47.570
Don't start getting cocky just because you play a popular policeman on TV!

00:08:47.570 --> 00:08:49.900
Can't you tell the difference between "hi" and "shi"?

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:55.250
I want you to practice walking bent-over like an old man until you can do it perfectly!

00:08:56.090 --> 00:09:00.630
The reason you can't do it is because you have no talent!

00:09:00.630 --> 00:09:02.340
You need to get out of acting!

00:09:04.420 --> 00:09:06.860
Any actor who quits over things like that...

00:09:06.860 --> 00:09:08.510
doesn't have what it takes to be in a theatrical masterpiece anyway!

00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:11.420
I'll leave them to you, then.

00:09:11.420 --> 00:09:17.760
We've actually decided to put on another blockbuster, Kuronuma.

00:09:26.140 --> 00:09:27.040
What?!

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:30.140
Madoka Enjouji is going to put on a play here?

00:09:30.470 --> 00:09:33.840
She's only recently been in the papers because she left the Hoshika Troupe!

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:36.190
This is her first play after leaving that troupe.

00:09:36.950 --> 00:09:39.380
Miss Enjouji, you are performing in <i>Isadora</i>, correct?

00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:40.640
What are your feelings on the play?

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:43.260
I want to make it a feast for the audience.

00:09:43.260 --> 00:09:46.650
Keeping an eye on the upcoming Acting Festival, the life of the legendary singer-dancer Isadora Duncan...

00:09:47.300 --> 00:09:50.160
is the role I'm devoting myself to.

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:51.650
The Acting Festival...

00:09:53.430 --> 00:09:57.780
We're aiming to win an award with one of our plays at the Acting Festival.

00:09:58.370 --> 00:10:01.630
We wanted to see which play to put forward...

00:10:01.630 --> 00:10:06.680
as our entry: <i>Isadora</i> or your <i>The Forgotten Wilderness</i>.

00:10:06.680 --> 00:10:10.720
I wish you luck.

00:10:18.540 --> 00:10:21.350
This is our new rehearsal space?

00:10:22.060 --> 00:10:26.350
Why do we have to move about for <i>Isadora</i>?

00:10:32.950 --> 00:10:35.680
How can we concentrate in a place like this?!

00:10:48.320 --> 00:10:49.430
Maya...

00:11:00.290 --> 00:11:03.060
Ayumi, is that really you?

00:11:03.440 --> 00:11:06.020
I hope I'm not calling in at a bad time.

00:11:06.020 --> 00:11:07.930
No, of course not!

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:11.840
Mr. Onodera is at my house right now.

00:11:11.840 --> 00:11:17.760
We know where Ms. Tsukikage is, but not her exact location.

00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:20.770
He said Mr. Hayami knows the details.

00:11:20.770 --> 00:11:22.880
Hasn't he told you anything?

00:11:23.360 --> 00:11:25.010
That heartless jerk!

00:11:25.010 --> 00:11:28.640
He said he would tell me as soon as he had news!

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:34.560
I'm sorry, but you need an appointment to see Mr. Hayami.

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:36.640
This is very important!

00:11:36.640 --> 00:11:38.340
Wait a minute!

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:40.580
Someone, stop that girl!

00:11:40.580 --> 00:11:42.360
I'm not going to interfere with his meeting!

00:11:42.340 --> 00:11:44.230
I just want to wait for him until he comes out.

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:52.440
That's no way to treat a girl.

00:11:52.700 --> 00:11:54.060
Miss Shiori.

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:55.810
I apologize.

00:11:57.390 --> 00:11:58.470
Are you all right?

00:12:00.850 --> 00:12:02.350
Why don't you use this?

00:12:02.670 --> 00:12:04.970
What is this racket?

00:12:05.910 --> 00:12:06.990
Little one.

00:12:07.770 --> 00:12:10.280
So, you were the mini typhoon that blew in here.

00:12:10.280 --> 00:12:11.400
What are you doing here?

00:12:11.400 --> 00:12:14.150
You'll know why I'm here if I tell you I want to talk about...

00:12:14.150 --> 00:12:15.470
Ms. Tsukikage.

00:12:17.980 --> 00:12:19.750
Why don't you step this way?

00:12:19.750 --> 00:12:22.070
He'll talk to you when he's finished up here.

00:12:26.490 --> 00:12:29.510
That's her, isn't it, Miss Mizuki?

00:12:29.510 --> 00:12:31.980
Mr. Hayami's...

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:32.970
That's right.

00:12:33.990 --> 00:12:35.760
What kind of a woman is she?

00:12:36.070 --> 00:12:39.230
Miss Shiori is an heiress to the Takamiya Group.

00:12:39.230 --> 00:12:41.280
She is President Takamiya's granddaughter.

00:12:42.160 --> 00:12:43.980
What exactly is the Takamiya Group?

00:12:43.980 --> 00:12:46.600
Construction, food production, railways,

00:12:46.600 --> 00:12:48.540
department stores and hotels.

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:51.960
The Takamiya group operates in various markets.

00:12:53.470 --> 00:12:57.980
Central TV and the Central newspaper are also part of their group.

00:12:57.980 --> 00:13:01.410
For Daito Entertainment, an alliance between Miss Shiori...

00:13:01.410 --> 00:13:04.530
and Mr. Masumi would be invaluable, which is why his father...

00:13:04.530 --> 00:13:07.550
is praying for this marriage to go ahead.

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:09.350
And how does Mr. Hayami feel about it?

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:15.850
He said for a long time that he'd only choose someone who would benefit Daito Entertainment.

00:13:17.420 --> 00:13:18.860
I guess he would say that, wouldn't he?

00:13:20.550 --> 00:13:21.880
Sorry I kept you waiting.

00:13:21.880 --> 00:13:24.140
Then, go ahead: Tell me what you wanted to say.

00:13:25.090 --> 00:13:30.100
What's wrong? You've gone all quiet. What happened to your spunk?

00:13:30.540 --> 00:13:35.060
If you know where Ms. Tsukikage is, please tell me!

00:13:35.430 --> 00:13:38.970
Please don't worry about it anymore. She's doing just fine.

00:13:39.280 --> 00:13:41.720
So, you've met up with her?!

00:13:41.980 --> 00:13:44.630
No, I haven't, but I sent someone to find her.

00:13:44.940 --> 00:13:49.080
All I can tell you right now is that she's in the home of <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>.

00:13:49.080 --> 00:13:51.590
The home of <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>?

00:13:52.300 --> 00:13:55.310
The region that <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>'s set was modeled on.

00:13:55.310 --> 00:13:59.000
It's a strange valley where plum trees don't make their vibrant last stand in February,

00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:00.840
but instead, stay in bloom until the beginning of summer.

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:04.990
They say there are so many wild plum blossoms there, the whole valley turns red.

00:14:07.270 --> 00:14:11.930
Ms. Tsukikage told me that she doesn't want me to announce her whereabouts.

00:14:12.390 --> 00:14:16.700
She was quite insistent that I should not reveal her location to you until next spring.

00:14:17.150 --> 00:14:19.340
Until next spring?

00:14:20.010 --> 00:14:26.570
If I don't receive an acting award by then, <i>The Scarlet Angel</i> will automatically go to Ayumi!

00:14:27.520 --> 00:14:31.430
It looks like <i>The Forgotten Wilderness</i> will be the play that tips the scales.

00:14:32.550 --> 00:14:37.070
I'm not going to give in even if I only have a one percent chance!

00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:41.310
I will also place all my hopes and expectations into that one percent of yours.

00:14:41.710 --> 00:14:43.120
I have faith in you.

00:14:44.520 --> 00:14:47.480
Sir, it's about time to get going.

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:55.520
Apparently, the home of <i>The Scarlet Angel</i> is a beautiful place indeed.

00:14:55.920 --> 00:14:58.790
They say that the night sky is awash with stars.

00:14:59.570 --> 00:15:04.390
Many of the stars you can see there can usually only be seen in a planetarium.

00:15:19.530 --> 00:15:24.540
I'd like to see the home of <i>The Scarlet Angel</i> at some point.

00:15:25.090 --> 00:15:26.450
I would like to see it as well.

00:15:30.390 --> 00:15:33.490
Well, I'm not going there with <i>you</i>!

00:15:33.490 --> 00:15:35.200
Who said I was going with you anyway?

00:15:36.170 --> 00:15:38.870
You think I want to take care of a kid?

00:15:39.010 --> 00:15:41.300
I'm not a kid anymore!

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:44.290
I've known you since you were in junior high.

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:45.600
Our president...

00:15:45.600 --> 00:15:47.310
...is having a war of words with a teenage girl.

00:15:47.610 --> 00:15:50.130
I don't want to
hear that from the
likes of you!

00:15:47.620 --> 00:15:50.130
Well, maybe if
you started acting
your age...

00:15:51.340 --> 00:15:52.810
Mr. Masumi.

00:15:54.960 --> 00:15:55.820
Are you all right?

00:15:55.820 --> 00:15:58.890
I'm sorry. It's my anemia again.

00:16:01.480 --> 00:16:03.700
I'll be going then.

00:16:03.700 --> 00:16:04.750
Hold it right there.

00:16:05.540 --> 00:16:10.210
The time I went to the planetarium with you was the last time.

00:16:11.050 --> 00:16:15.570
I won't go there again, probably for the rest of my life.

00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:18.920
Mr. Hayami?

00:16:27.270 --> 00:16:29.280
She's got such an overwhelming presence!

00:16:29.850 --> 00:16:31.440
Wow!

00:16:31.440 --> 00:16:34.090
That's Takeshi Furuhata, the famous stage designer!

00:16:34.090 --> 00:16:38.070
And that woman is the internationally-acclaimed dancer and choreographer, Mirei Tachibana!

00:16:38.070 --> 00:16:42.120
And they've got Russel, that light technician who's worked on loads of Broadway hits!

00:16:42.120 --> 00:16:43.590
What a group!

00:16:45.630 --> 00:16:49.400
Hey, have you guys heard? I guess the show at Kinyuu Hall is getting canceled.

00:16:51.970 --> 00:16:53.560
Is that true, sir?

00:16:53.560 --> 00:16:56.480
Is the show at Kinyuu Hall really getting canceled?

00:16:56.650 --> 00:17:01.340
The president is looking for a stage that can support a lower budget.

00:17:01.340 --> 00:17:04.920
I can't believe they're putting all their resources into <i>Isadora</i>.

00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:07.390
Are they trying to make our play go under?

00:17:07.390 --> 00:17:09.480
I'll go and negotiate with the president!

00:17:09.480 --> 00:17:11.290
It won't do you any good!

00:17:11.290 --> 00:17:14.230
I've met with him time and time again and this is the result.

00:17:16.480 --> 00:17:21.120
We have no specified performance space or performance time now, but I'm not going to give up!

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:23.000
I won't be unreasonable!

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:25.210
Anyone who wants to quit now is free to leave.

00:17:25.780 --> 00:17:30.900
I only want those who say they still want to act with me under these conditions to stay!

00:17:30.900 --> 00:17:32.420
Sir...

00:17:37.840 --> 00:17:41.110
I can't believe nearly all of the actors ended up quitting.

00:17:41.110 --> 00:17:44.850
Well, it really helps that my costar hasn't quit.

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:48.850
I would never quit, no matter what!

00:17:49.600 --> 00:17:53.940
I'm going to find more actors - actors who fit my vision!

00:17:53.940 --> 00:17:55.340
Mr. Kuronuma!

00:17:55.340 --> 00:18:01.020
I love acting, which is why I want to treat my play right.

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:05.670
Hey, look! It's Ryuuzo Kuronuma.

00:18:05.670 --> 00:18:10.200
They say that all but two of his actors have boycotted him.

00:18:10.200 --> 00:18:12.980
How does he expect to put a play together like that?!

00:18:13.760 --> 00:18:17.220
They're out there somewhere!

00:18:18.420 --> 00:18:20.270
My actors!

00:18:27.180 --> 00:18:29.340
How can I help you, Mr. President?

00:18:29.340 --> 00:18:32.940
You are our younger staff's number one and I need your help.

00:18:34.160 --> 00:18:41.120
Would you be willing to audition for the role of Enjouji Madoka's lover in the play <i>Isadora</i>?

00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:47.680
You were picked by Miss Enjouji herself and <i>Isadora</i> is going to be hot stuff.

00:18:47.680 --> 00:18:50.350
This is a rare opportunity.

00:18:50.700 --> 00:18:52.430
I'm sorry, but...

00:18:53.900 --> 00:18:56.140
May I take up some of your time,

00:18:57.660 --> 00:18:59.560
Sakurakouji?

00:19:01.180 --> 00:19:08.390
Everybody, let me introduce you: This is our most popular teen star, Yuu Sakurakouji.

00:19:09.170 --> 00:19:12.920
He's passionate, handsome, and a little naive.

00:19:12.920 --> 00:19:14.140
What do you think?

00:19:14.580 --> 00:19:19.650
Don't you think he'd be perfect for the role of Isadora's lover?

00:19:22.750 --> 00:19:26.650
What? Sakurakouji is joining <i>Isadora</i> in the role of Isadora's lover?!

00:19:27.130 --> 00:19:31.400
He was seen at a restaurant near here, surrounded by Miss Enjouji and the Isadora staff...

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:32.940
and they were all talking about it.

00:19:33.680 --> 00:19:35.120
I can't believe it!

00:19:35.720 --> 00:19:36.960
Maya!

00:19:59.840 --> 00:20:02.130
Maya, what are you doing out here?

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:04.470
You're soaked!

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:08.990
How am I supposed to play Jane without Stewart?!

00:20:09.860 --> 00:20:10.880
Maya!

00:20:12.090 --> 00:20:15.130
Please don't leave me all alone!

00:20:17.300 --> 00:20:19.360
I rejected the <i>Isadora</i> offer.

00:20:19.750 --> 00:20:23.490
I'm doing <i>The Forgotten Wilderness</i> with you.

00:20:24.150 --> 00:20:28.210
I'm not going anywhere. No matter what happens.

00:20:29.890 --> 00:20:31.440
So, that's what he said?

00:20:31.440 --> 00:20:32.810
It's an insult!

00:20:32.810 --> 00:20:37.310
He would rather act with some girl called Maya Kitajima than me!

00:20:38.710 --> 00:20:42.390
I think it was meant as an insult, Miss Enjouji.

00:20:42.390 --> 00:20:43.520
What?

00:20:43.820 --> 00:20:46.720
You're up against Maya Kitajima.

00:20:46.720 --> 00:20:48.770
You know <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>, right?

00:20:48.770 --> 00:20:51.010
Of course I do.

00:20:51.520 --> 00:20:54.890
Well, Maya Kitajima counts Chigusa Tsukikage as her mentor...

00:20:54.890 --> 00:20:57.060
and she's considered to be a contender for the starring role in <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>.

00:20:57.700 --> 00:20:58.940
You can't be serious!

00:20:58.940 --> 00:21:03.130
Not long ago, she played Puck the fairy on Kichijouji's outdoor stage...

00:21:03.130 --> 00:21:05.450
in a production of <i>A Midsummer Night's Dream</i>...

00:21:12.950 --> 00:21:17.730
that she put on with her friends, and they managed to attract a crowd of six thousand over a three-day stint.

00:21:17.730 --> 00:21:19.230
Six thousand?!

00:21:19.230 --> 00:21:22.590
That's the kind of actor Sakurakouji chose.

00:21:34.290 --> 00:21:37.540
Open Casting for <i>The Forgotten Wilderness</i>

00:21:36.230 --> 00:21:41.580
Abandoned by most of the other actors, Maya and Sakurakouji are facing a dilemma.

00:21:41.580 --> 00:21:46.220
Will Ryuuzo Kuronuma be able to go up against <i>Isadora</i> and actually stage...

00:21:46.220 --> 00:21:49.910
<i>The Forgotten Wilderness</i>?

00:21:51.650 --> 00:21:56.680
Hello hello

00:21:51.650 --> 00:21:56.680
Hello, hello.

00:22:04.150 --> 00:22:15.280
Fukanou dato iwarenagara tobitatte

00:22:04.150 --> 00:22:15.280
Even though they say it's impossible, I fly off.

00:22:15.280 --> 00:22:25.160
Kanaeta yume mo koboreochita yume mo aru

00:22:15.280 --> 00:22:25.160
There are dreams that come true, and dreams that crumble away.

00:22:25.160 --> 00:22:36.830
Soredemo isshoukenmei ikiru kazu dake hoshi ga fueru

00:22:25.160 --> 00:22:36.830
But even then, for every person trying hard to live their life, a new star is born.

00:22:36.830 --> 00:22:49.240
Kyou mo mata hitotsu umareru hoshi miagete

00:22:36.830 --> 00:22:49.240
Today, I look up again, at another newly born star.

00:22:49.240 --> 00:22:50.570
And I say,

00:22:49.240 --> 00:22:50.570
And I say,

00:22:50.570 --> 00:22:53.890
Hello hello another star

00:22:50.570 --> 00:22:53.890
Hello, hello another star.

00:22:53.890 --> 00:22:57.030
If I wish anything will change

00:22:53.890 --> 00:22:57.030
If I wish anything will change.

00:22:57.030 --> 00:23:02.770
Ai wo daite norikonda shatoru

00:22:57.030 --> 00:23:02.770
I've boarded the shuttle with my love.

00:23:02.770 --> 00:23:09.120
Daremo ga hitori no uchuuhikoushi dayo

00:23:02.770 --> 00:23:09.120
Every single person is an astronaut.

00:23:09.120 --> 00:23:14.190
Negau yume kara yume e

00:23:09.120 --> 00:23:14.190
From fulfilled dream to dream,

00:23:14.190 --> 00:23:21.470
Dokomademo yukeru one life

00:23:14.190 --> 00:23:21.470
I can go anywhere... One life.

00:23:22.490 --> 00:23:26.330
We have a new cast now, thanks to the open auditions.

00:23:26.740 --> 00:23:29.920
Even though they're all inexperienced, they fit their roles perfectly...

00:23:29.920 --> 00:23:31.420
and the play has become very fun.

00:23:31.860 --> 00:23:35.290
Mr. Kuronuma is a great director!

00:23:35.760 --> 00:23:37.740
I'm going to have to work hard too.

00:23:38.130 --> 00:23:42.710
But how can I capture the expression of a wild wolf?

00:23:43.720 --> 00:23:46.190
I don't understand Jane's heart at all.

00:23:47.250 --> 00:23:51.500
Episode 41 - Wild Heart
